Portly shows what uses local TCP and UDP ports, which project it belongs to, and stops it safely.

Usage:
  portly [port ...] [flags]
  portly [command]

Examples:
  portly                    list ports
  portly 8000               details for a port
  portly 8000/udp           only UDP
  portly stop 8000          stop it, after asking
  portly update             update to the latest release
  portly --json             for scripts and agents

Available Commands:
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help        Help about any command
  stop        Stop what uses a port, after showing it and asking
  update      Update portly to the latest release

Flags:
      --all       also list likely-client UDP ports
  -h, --help      help for portly
      --json      print one JSON document
      --verbose   print diagnostics on stderr
  -v, --version   version for portly

Use "portly [command] --help" for more information about a command.
